It is difficult to represent that elliptical illocution though. Either 
{ge'e} can represent an illocution or evidential as well, which makes it 
extremely vague, or it can only express UI1-type emotions, in which case it 
isn't useful here. On the other hand, there may not be enough justification 
to create a cmavo to represent it.

Or perhaps we could just take a page from Curtis and create a ridiculously 
long cmavo so as to not take up space that we might want to actually use, 
e.g. {ju'a'o'e} :p

